cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: >-
  Explainable AI to Guide the Design of Interpretable Prediction Models From High-Dimensional Data, Applied to Falls and Related Injuries in Adults Aged 50 Years or Older: Algorithm Development and Validation
abstract: >-
  Code for the Exploratory AI Recommender: feature attributions of a random
  survival forest are turned into recommendations (features to exclude,
  non-linear terms and pairwise interactions) for a Cox proportional hazards
  model, which is then evaluated on held-out data. The repository contains the
  recommendation and evaluation code used for the main (DataLoch) analysis,
  demonstrations on three open data sets (GBSG2, ACT and peakVO2), additional
  analyses on those data sets, and simulations of the recommendation rules.
  The data processing specific to DataLoch is not included.
